1
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:06,267
This is a quarter of a million euros. And
this is how it dies.

2
00:00:07,533 --> 00:00:12,216
No first call in twenty-four hours. No
next action. No decision.

3
00:00:12,216 --> 00:00:16,533
Thirty days of silence, while the alerts
watched it happen.

4
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:18,733
It never had to happen.

5
00:00:20,467 --> 00:00:23,133
Every RM starts the day with competing
signals.

6
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:27,714
A first contact coming due. A next action
already overdue.

7
00:00:27,714 --> 00:00:31,351
A follow-up to send. A deal with no next
step at all.

8
00:00:31,351 --> 00:00:36,567
An internal request still open. And a
calendar with less room than it looks.

9
00:00:37,567 --> 00:00:39,859
Every RM starts with competing signals.

10
00:00:39,859 --> 00:00:42,033
The work is knowing what moves first.

11
00:00:52,367 --> 00:00:55,183
SalesMind is EXANTE's RM workspace.

12
00:00:55,183 --> 00:00:59,367
One place for your book, your pipeline and
your day.

13
00:00:59,967 --> 00:01:05,184
Your deals. Your tasks. What your clients
did. How you are performing.

14
00:01:05,184 --> 00:01:09,953
Your sales plan. Your requests to internal
teams. The guidebook.

15
00:01:09,953 --> 00:01:11,444
The sales materials.

16
00:01:11,444 --> 00:01:15,767
And, once you connect it, your calendar
beside your tasks.

17
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:22,258
It reads from the CRM and writes back to
it. So treat every click as real.

18
00:01:22,258 --> 00:01:27,667
Qualification you fill in, and loss
reasons you choose, land in the CRM.

19
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:36,415
The screen you are seeing is a synthetic
training environment.

20
00:01:36,415 --> 00:01:37,867
No live client data is used.

21
00:01:38,467 --> 00:01:42,188
You sign in, and your workspace opens on
the left-hand menu.

22
00:01:42,188 --> 00:01:43,367
It has four groups.

23
00:01:43,967 --> 00:01:48,033
Workspace holds the Dashboard, Task
management and Internal requests.

24
00:01:48,633 --> 00:01:51,833
Book holds Pipeline, Clients and Activity.

25
00:01:52,433 --> 00:01:54,467
Results holds Performance and Bonus.

26
00:01:55,067 --> 00:01:59,000
Support holds the Guidebook, Sales
materials and the Changelog.

27
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:03,306
Across the top: Search, for pages and
clients. Change theme.

28
00:02:03,306 --> 00:02:04,665
And your account menu.

29
00:02:04,665 --> 00:02:08,000
The menu collapses at its foot when you
need the room.

30
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:12,100
Eleven pages. Most days, you work in a
handful of them.

31
00:02:13,033 --> 00:02:16,322
Before your first real day, clean the book
once.

32
00:02:16,322 --> 00:02:19,611
Check every deal is real and at the right
stage.

33
00:02:19,611 --> 00:02:23,996
Tidy duplicates and old blockers. Give
everything a next action.

34
00:02:23,996 --> 00:02:27,833
One to two hours, once. Then the routine
keeps it clean.

35
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:36,000
Start here. This is the control surface.

36
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:39,286
Across the top, your active milestone:

37
00:02:39,286 --> 00:02:44,377
liquid NAV against the target, what
remains, and the date it is checked.

38
00:02:44,377 --> 00:02:49,608
Beside it, net new money for the year
against your goal. Then three tiles.

39
00:02:49,608 --> 00:02:52,365
My clients. Total NAV. Open deal value.

40
00:02:52,365 --> 00:02:55,900
Click Open deal value and you are in the
Pipeline.

41
00:02:56,833 --> 00:03:02,018
Below sits the list that runs your
morning. Four tabs. Going quiet.

42
00:03:02,018 --> 00:03:05,500
New opportunities. Open deals. Open
requests.

43
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:09,200
Open deals are already sorted, most urgent
first.

44
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:15,203
Critical alerts. Then overdue next
actions. Then deals with no next action.

45
00:03:15,203 --> 00:03:19,454
Then deals past the stage's time limit.
Then blocked deals.

46
00:03:19,454 --> 00:03:20,967
Then everything else.

47
00:03:22,167 --> 00:03:24,467
Sort by urgency. Work from the top.

48
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,267
On the right, recent activity.

49
00:03:28,267 --> 00:03:31,691
Switch between the last seven days and the
last thirty.

50
00:03:31,691 --> 00:03:33,433
View all opens the full log.

51
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:42,166
Task management is where a task and an
hour become the same thing.

52
00:03:42,766 --> 00:03:48,533
Three tabs, in the order you use them.
Inbox. Today. Planning.

53
00:03:49,133 --> 00:03:52,417
The Inbox holds everything without a day
yet.

54
00:03:52,417 --> 00:03:55,848
Tasks you captured, and the emails you
starred.

55
00:03:55,848 --> 00:04:01,322
Pick one, read it in the pane on the
right, and give it a day. Today. Week.

56
00:04:01,322 --> 00:04:04,533
Month. Or Later. The keys are T, W, M and
L.

57
00:04:05,466 --> 00:04:08,738
To capture, press C, type one line and
press Enter.

58
00:04:08,738 --> 00:04:13,100
An at sign links a client. A time makes it
a block on your calendar.

59
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:16,500
An exclamation mark sets the horizon or
the priority.

60
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:18,466
Give the task a day.

61
00:04:19,066 --> 00:04:22,333
Today shows your list beside your
calendar.

62
00:04:22,333 --> 00:04:27,879
Each task carries its age, its time if it
has one, and how long it takes.

63
00:04:27,879 --> 00:04:30,766
Filter by client. Undo with Control Z.

64
00:04:31,366 --> 00:04:35,948
Once a day, run Plan the day. First,
yesterday as it really went.

65
00:04:35,948 --> 00:04:36,948
Then today,

66
00:04:36,724 --> 00:04:41,306
with a ring that shows how much of the day
is already spoken for.

67
00:04:41,306 --> 00:04:44,266
Clear the Inbox. Fill Today. Start my day.

68
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:49,293
Planning shows what is further out, as a
board or a list.

69
00:04:49,293 --> 00:04:53,733
Inbox, Today, Coming week, Coming month,
Later, Blocked and Done.

70
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:02,681
The Pipeline holds your deals, and only
yours. Three tabs.

71
00:05:02,681 --> 00:05:05,940
New Business, for clients who have not
funded yet.

72
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:10,634
Client Growth, for new money from clients
who have. And your Sales plan.

73
00:05:11,234 --> 00:05:14,004
The toolbar: Search client. Filters.

74
00:05:14,004 --> 00:05:19,543
Closed window, which sets how far back
closed deals stay visible. Views.

75
00:05:19,543 --> 00:05:21,467
Sort. And Board or Table.

76
00:05:22,067 --> 00:05:27,429
The fastest filters are the focus chips.
Overdue. Due this week.

77
00:05:27,429 --> 00:05:31,367
No contact in thirty days or more. With
amount.

78
00:05:31,967 --> 00:05:35,894
Every morning, open Filters, then Alert,
then Has alert.

79
00:05:35,894 --> 00:05:37,927
Overdue actions are included.

80
00:05:37,927 --> 00:05:41,434
Save it under Views, and it is one click
tomorrow.

81
00:05:42,034 --> 00:05:46,656
Alerts tell you where to look first. Four
are critical: SLA breach,

82
00:05:46,656 --> 00:05:50,451
Stopped responding to onboarding, Funding
not arriving,

83
00:05:50,451 --> 00:05:55,626
and Qualification missing. The warnings
are Lead untouched, Action overdue,

84
00:05:55,626 --> 00:06:00,180
Rescheduled repeatedly, Check contact
details, and Back from Lost.

85
00:06:00,180 --> 00:06:02,595
Suspected duplicate is information.

86
00:06:02,595 --> 00:06:07,700
Alerts clear by themselves once you fix
the problem. Back from Lost stays.

87
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:12,668
The clock that matters most is first
contact. Inbound leads:

88
00:06:12,668 --> 00:06:14,992
twenty-four hours, weekends excluded.

89
00:06:14,992 --> 00:06:19,764
Assigned Friday at three, due Monday at
three. Outbound: one calendar month.

90
00:06:19,764 --> 00:06:22,967
Contact late, and the deal is marked late
for good.

91
00:06:24,034 --> 00:06:30,003
No answer? Follow the schedule. Day zero,
call and email. Day one, call.

92
00:06:30,003 --> 00:06:33,568
Day three, call and email. Day seven,
call:

93
00:06:33,568 --> 00:06:39,786
the last step for outbound leads. Day
twelve, a break-up email for inbound.

94
00:06:39,786 --> 00:06:43,600
Then decide whether to close the deal as
Lost.

95
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:46,348
One more dialog to know.

96
00:06:46,348 --> 00:06:50,411
Moving a deal into Contact Established
with no reply on record,

97
00:06:50,411 --> 00:06:54,022
SalesMind asks how you reached them. Pick
what happened.

98
00:06:54,022 --> 00:06:56,795
That records the contact in SalesMind
only.

99
00:06:56,795 --> 00:07:01,567
Keeping a marketing lead still takes a
call logged as answered in the CRM.

100
00:07:07,234 --> 00:07:09,834
On the board, each column is a stage,

101
00:07:09,834 --> 00:07:13,067
with its count and its total expected
deposit.

102
00:07:13,667 --> 00:07:19,622
New Business runs from New Opportunity, to
Contact Established, Qualified,

103
00:07:19,622 --> 00:07:24,772
Solution Presented, Onboarding, Funding
Pending, Funded and Won.

104
00:07:24,772 --> 00:07:27,267
Lost and On Hold sit alongside.

105
00:07:27,867 --> 00:07:32,066
Most of it moves by itself. A reply, a
call over ten seconds,

106
00:07:32,066 --> 00:07:35,301
or an accepted invite moves New
Opportunity on.

107
00:07:35,301 --> 00:07:40,188
A submitted application, a passed KYC and
arriving money move the rest.

108
00:07:40,188 --> 00:07:42,941
You move the stages that need judgement.

109
00:07:42,941 --> 00:07:46,934
New Business Funded, and every Won, are
never set by hand.

110
00:07:48,067 --> 00:07:52,189
A card answers three questions. How long
in this stage.

111
00:07:52,189 --> 00:07:55,111
How long since contact. How much money.

112
00:07:55,111 --> 00:07:58,634
Days in stage turns bold when the deal is
late.

113
00:07:59,234 --> 00:08:01,185
Switch to Table for a review.

114
00:08:01,185 --> 00:08:05,827
The next stage action shows in violet
while it is still a suggestion.

115
00:08:05,827 --> 00:08:10,267
The first contact column says Met, Late,
Overdue, or the due date.

116
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:13,557
Client Growth has its own stages.

117
00:08:13,557 --> 00:08:18,843
Discovery, Validation, Negotiation,
Approval, In Progress, Funded and Won.

118
00:08:18,843 --> 00:08:21,700
You move every one of them up to Funded.

119
00:08:26,834 --> 00:08:30,439
The screen you are seeing is a synthetic
training environment.

120
00:08:30,439 --> 00:08:32,067
No live client data is used.

121
00:08:32,667 --> 00:08:36,904
This is Northstar Capital Training, a
training deal at Contact Established,

122
00:08:36,904 --> 00:08:40,067
with an expected deposit of five hundred
thousand euros.

123
00:08:40,667 --> 00:08:45,330
On the left: the stage, the money, the
account lifecycle, and qualification.

124
00:08:45,330 --> 00:08:46,330
On the right:

125
00:08:46,127 --> 00:08:50,667
About this deal, the next stage action,
the blocker, and the latest notes.

126
00:08:51,267 --> 00:08:54,301
Every active deal has exactly one next
action.

127
00:08:54,301 --> 00:08:56,477
SalesMind suggests it, in violet.

128
00:08:56,477 --> 00:09:00,434
Change the words or the date if you need
to. Then accept it.

129
00:09:01,434 --> 00:09:05,534
Accept the next action. It becomes your
task, with its due date.

130
00:09:07,334 --> 00:09:10,925
When it is done, mark it complete. Say
what happened.

131
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:12,484
Add a note if it helps.

132
00:09:12,484 --> 00:09:16,685
Set the next action, because a deal is
never left without one.

133
00:09:16,685 --> 00:09:19,667
Here, choose Complete and move to
Qualified.

134
00:09:20,867 --> 00:09:24,012
If something is missing, the move dialog
tells you.

135
00:09:24,012 --> 00:09:25,800
It is a reminder, not a wall.

136
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:30,320
Need a reminder about the client that is
not the deal's next step?

137
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,567
Add an ordinary task.

138
00:09:32,167 --> 00:09:34,484
The client is real, but not now?

139
00:09:34,484 --> 00:09:39,553
Put the deal on hold, with a reason and,
if you can, a follow-up date.

140
00:09:39,553 --> 00:09:44,912
It is over? Close the deal, pick the loss
reason with care, and write why.

141
00:09:44,912 --> 00:09:46,867
The reason goes to the CRM.

142
00:09:47,467 --> 00:09:49,667
Do not leave an important deal without a
next move.

143
00:09:55,633 --> 00:09:58,867
Client Growth is new money from clients
who have already funded.

144
00:09:59,467 --> 00:10:02,635
On the Client Growth tab, click Create
deal.

145
00:10:02,635 --> 00:10:06,091
Type three or more letters of the client's
name.

146
00:10:06,091 --> 00:10:11,420
Pick Meridian Family Office Demo, and the
type. Brokerage, or White label.

147
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:14,300
Add the expected deposit if you know it.

148
00:10:14,900 --> 00:10:19,200
A funded client gets a deal at Discovery,
with a suggested next action.

149
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:22,328
If the client already has an open deal,

150
00:10:22,328 --> 00:10:26,800
SalesMind will not open a second one. Edit
the existing deal instead.

151
00:10:27,733 --> 00:10:33,483
From there you move it. Discovery.
Validation. Negotiation. Approval.

152
00:10:33,483 --> 00:10:35,150
In Progress. Funded.

153
00:10:35,150 --> 00:10:40,400
Once deposits reach the expected deposit,
Won is set by itself.

154
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:45,608
Open the deal, and the expected deposit
panel shows how far you are.

155
00:10:45,608 --> 00:10:49,404
The schedule from the CRM. Every deposit
and withdrawal.

156
00:10:49,404 --> 00:10:51,233
And the amount still to go.

157
00:10:52,233 --> 00:10:55,915
And one piece of housekeeping. A client
works one deal.

158
00:10:55,915 --> 00:10:59,797
If old data left several open, an amber
button lists them.

159
00:10:59,797 --> 00:11:04,349
Keep the right one, and close the rest as
duplicates. One exception:

160
00:11:04,349 --> 00:11:08,833
if a White Label deal is involved, choose
Later, and close nothing.

161
00:11:14,633 --> 00:11:18,170
The screen you are seeing is a synthetic
training environment.

162
00:11:18,170 --> 00:11:19,767
No live client data is used.

163
00:11:20,367 --> 00:11:23,910
Clients lists your book. All, Clients or
Contacts.

164
00:11:23,910 --> 00:11:29,295
Quick filters for high value, high risk
and not funded. Compact or detailed.

165
00:11:29,295 --> 00:11:31,633
Filters, columns and saved views.

166
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:35,033
Before you approach anyone new, check
ownership.

167
00:11:35,633 --> 00:11:40,395
Search by full name, exact email or phone,
or the company domain.

168
00:11:40,395 --> 00:11:42,667
One search returns one verdict.

169
00:11:43,267 --> 00:11:47,664
Available. Free to approach. Claimed.
Another RM owns them.

170
00:11:47,664 --> 00:11:51,539
Request reassignment if you have a case.
Restricted.

171
00:11:51,539 --> 00:11:56,979
A funded client or a protected company. Do
not approach. Needs narrowing.

172
00:11:56,979 --> 00:12:00,109
Add the domain or a full email. Not found.

173
00:12:00,109 --> 00:12:04,133
Add the contact to the CRM, and it is
assigned to you.

174
00:12:05,533 --> 00:12:07,600
You have one hundred searches a day.

175
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,400
Check ownership before approaching the
contact.

176
00:12:11,667 --> 00:12:18,203
Available? Then make the lead yours. It
enters the CRM on the Contacts tab.

177
00:12:18,203 --> 00:12:23,171
Name. Email or phone, one of the two.
Phone, digits only.

178
00:12:23,171 --> 00:12:28,314
Individual, or corporate. If the CRM
refuses the add, stop:

179
00:12:28,314 --> 00:12:31,800
that lead already belongs to another RM.

180
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:36,004
A whole list goes in as one plain-text
spreadsheet,

181
00:12:36,004 --> 00:12:40,715
with your email in the Manager column, so
every lead lands under your name.

182
00:12:40,715 --> 00:12:42,349
And leads are not forever.

183
00:12:42,349 --> 00:12:45,867
Left untouched for six months, a lead can
be reassigned.

184
00:12:46,867 --> 00:12:50,561
From there, the lead walks the CRM's own
path. Contacts.

185
00:12:50,561 --> 00:12:53,333
Registrants, when they sign up. Qualified,

186
00:12:53,333 --> 00:12:59,073
once the ten qualification tags are filled and
an answered call or a meeting is logged.

187
00:12:59,073 --> 00:13:03,559
Compliance requires that before
onboarding. Then Waiting for Review.

188
00:13:03,559 --> 00:13:04,813
KYC passed. Funded.

189
00:13:04,813 --> 00:13:09,233
And the qualification you fill in
SalesMind writes those same tags.

190
00:13:15,233 --> 00:13:20,316
Activity is the full log of your book.
Emails, calls, meetings, deposits,

191
00:13:20,316 --> 00:13:23,936
withdrawals, registrations, KYC events and
requests.

192
00:13:23,936 --> 00:13:27,000
Topic tags tell you what each one was
about.

193
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:29,500
Open an item to read it in full.

194
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:33,794
If something was recorded wrong, raise an
issue from the item.

195
00:13:33,794 --> 00:13:37,369
Choose the category and the meeting type,
and write a short,

196
00:13:37,369 --> 00:13:41,600
factual comment. The team reviews it
within one to three business days.

197
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:46,367
Record the activity. If it is not in the
record, nobody else can see it.

198
00:13:52,167 --> 00:13:57,482
Performance is one page with six sections.
NAV milestones. Pipeline.

199
00:13:57,482 --> 00:14:01,000
Funding. Standing. Conversion.
Communication.

200
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:05,132
The period filter covers this month to all
time.

201
00:14:05,132 --> 00:14:10,503
NAV milestones follow your tenure instead:
own liquid NAV at month three,

202
00:14:10,503 --> 00:14:15,800
then total liquid NAV at six, twelve,
twenty-four and thirty-six months.

203
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,700
The figures you see here are synthetic.

204
00:14:23,866 --> 00:14:27,426
The screen you are seeing is a synthetic
training environment.

205
00:14:27,426 --> 00:14:29,033
No live client data is used.

206
00:14:29,633 --> 00:14:32,900
Your sales plan lives inside the Pipeline,
on its own tab.

207
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:38,132
Add an entry, and create the contact, or
link the CRM record.

208
00:14:38,132 --> 00:14:43,904
Every entry needs a valid CRM link, or a
written reason under Not Available.

209
00:14:43,904 --> 00:14:46,866
Be specific. N slash A is not a reason.

210
00:14:47,933 --> 00:14:51,141
New RMs finalise the plan within their
first ten days.

211
00:14:51,141 --> 00:14:52,566
It is a compliance step.

212
00:14:53,166 --> 00:14:57,861
Link an entry to a CRM contact and a deal
appears on the board at once.

213
00:14:57,861 --> 00:15:01,894
Filter by origin to see only plan deals.
Sales Plan Progress,

214
00:15:01,894 --> 00:15:06,257
Entries Requiring Attention, Forecasted
NAV, plan against reality,

215
00:15:06,257 --> 00:15:09,166
and plan history show where the plan
stands.

216
00:15:14,667 --> 00:15:18,046
The screen you are seeing is a simulated
permissions screen.

217
00:15:18,046 --> 00:15:19,567
No live connection is made.

218
00:15:20,167 --> 00:15:25,767
Connect Google once. Pick your work
account, continue, select all, continue.

219
00:15:26,367 --> 00:15:29,700
From then on, your real meetings sit
beside your tasks.

220
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:34,609
A task with a time becomes a block in a
separate calendar called SalesMind Tasks.

221
00:15:34,609 --> 00:15:37,276
Colleagues looking for a slot do not see
it.

222
00:15:37,276 --> 00:15:40,367
A meeting you create does go to your main
calendar.

223
00:15:41,434 --> 00:15:44,834
Deleting a time-blocked task deletes its
calendar block too.

224
00:15:45,434 --> 00:15:49,039
The screen you are seeing is a synthetic
training environment.

225
00:15:49,039 --> 00:15:50,667
No live client data is used.

226
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:59,406
When you are unsure, the Guidebook has
twenty short pages,

227
00:15:59,406 --> 00:16:03,634
from the new pipeline in one minute to the
cheat sheet and glossary.

228
00:16:04,234 --> 00:16:07,783
Sales materials collects the current
playbooks and battle cards.

229
00:16:07,783 --> 00:16:10,667
Use the latest version in every client
conversation.

230
00:16:11,267 --> 00:16:13,334
The Changelog tells you what changed.

231
00:16:13,934 --> 00:16:17,402
Internal requests shows your open Jira,
onboarding,

232
00:16:17,402 --> 00:16:21,619
KYC and Intercom requests. Raise a request
from the top right.

233
00:16:21,619 --> 00:16:25,700
Open requests on a client show up under
that deal's blocker.

234
00:16:26,634 --> 00:16:28,879
Onboarding can ask you, too.

235
00:16:28,879 --> 00:16:34,574
A monitoring request lands in the Requests
tab, and the clock is yours.

236
00:16:34,574 --> 00:16:40,669
Email the client within three days. No
answer in fourteen, call. Keep at it:

237
00:16:40,669 --> 00:16:42,434
thirty, sixty, ninety.

238
00:16:43,367 --> 00:16:47,452
Let it sit, and the statuses harden.
Document pending.

239
00:16:47,452 --> 00:16:49,192
Withdrawal restriction:

240
00:16:49,192 --> 00:16:54,715
funds go back only to the account the
deposit came from. Then Close only:

241
00:16:54,715 --> 00:16:58,800
no new positions. Deliver the documents,
and it lifts.

242
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:06,500
Close the day the same way every day.

243
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:11,699
Critical alerts cleared. First contact
deadlines protected.

244
00:17:11,699 --> 00:17:17,312
Overdue actions worked. Inbox triaged.
Today planned. Activity recorded.

245
00:17:17,312 --> 00:17:22,222
Ownership checked. Client Growth reviewed.
Sales Plan reviewed.

246
00:17:22,222 --> 00:17:27,133
Requests reviewed. Calendar capacity
checked. Tomorrow planned.

247
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:30,767
And every important deal has a next
action.

248
00:17:32,367 --> 00:17:36,087
The screen you are seeing is a synthetic
training environment.

249
00:17:36,087 --> 00:17:37,767
No live client data is used.

250
00:17:38,367 --> 00:17:40,900
Your book is under control when the next
action is clear.

251
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:51,252
One more thing. Everything you logged
today is evidence.

252
00:17:51,252 --> 00:17:54,867
Your review reads SalesMind and the CRM,
not your memory.

253
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:59,050
Meet Ollie, EXANTE's review assistant, in
beta.

254
00:17:59,050 --> 00:18:01,746
It lives in Slack, as a direct message.

255
00:18:01,746 --> 00:18:05,687
The screen you are seeing is a simulated
training screen.

256
00:18:05,687 --> 00:18:07,900
Every figure on it is synthetic.

257
00:18:08,500 --> 00:18:10,193
Ask it: how am I tracking.

258
00:18:10,193 --> 00:18:14,750
It answers with the target, the gap, and
your next agreement. Any day.

259
00:18:14,750 --> 00:18:16,833
No waiting for a review meeting.

260
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:21,678
Before a scheduled review, Ollie talks it
through with you.

261
00:18:21,678 --> 00:18:23,791
You agree, or you dispute a fact.

262
00:18:23,791 --> 00:18:27,633
Then it files the review, clearly marked
as filed by the AI.

263
00:18:28,633 --> 00:18:30,052
And the line that matters:

264
00:18:30,052 --> 00:18:33,433
committee decisions, pay and employment
are decided by people.

265
00:18:35,367 --> 00:18:38,892
So the loop closes. Log the work. Ollie
reads it.

266
00:18:38,892 --> 00:18:41,267
The review agrees your next step.
